<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wei Qing</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 106 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wei Qing was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a> general of the second century BCE who led major campaigns against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-han">Emperor Wu</a>. With his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huo-qubing">Huo Qubing</a>, he conducted the decisive northern campaigns that drove Xiongnu power beyond the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gobi-desert">Gobi Desert</a>. The Han Dynasty and Xiongnu Empire profiles treat these campaigns as a turning point in the long struggle between the two powers.</p></div>
